---
description: Coding standards and safe implementation
alwaysApply: true
---
- Follow existing naming, formatting, architecture, and folder conventions.
- Prefer small components and clear responsibilities.
- Reuse existing navigation, form, validation, persistence, and styling patterns.
- Avoid `any`, unsafe casts, duplicated constants, dead code, and unnecessary dependencies.
- Handle async operations and errors explicitly.
- Ensure controls have accessible labels, suitable touch targets, and visible interaction states.
- Never silence compiler, lint, or test errors to make a build appear successful.
- Do not replace working functionality with mock data or static UI.
- Add tests for business logic and critical user journeys.
